    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **28 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field, derived from an owner's city via a fixed city-to-region table.\n\nThe `locality` value is a pure function of the owner's own `city` \u2014 exactly like the existing derived fields `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipTier` \u2014 so it's computed at response-mapping time and needs no persistence or new pipeline steps.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `OwnerDto` schema, so the generated DTO carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` to `toOwnerDto`, backed by a fixed `CITY_REGIONS` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `locality(owner)` method that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` when the city isn't in the table.\n\nBoth new `Cp17Tests` cases pass (known city \u2192 `NSW`, unknown city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`), and all 28 existing tests remain green.",
